# rules: kotlin-mutable-pending-intent
# languages: kotlin
# fixture: kotlin/CWE-927.kt
# from: CWE-927 (Use of Implicit Intent for Sensitive Communication), CWE-926
#
# A PendingIntent is a token that lets whoever holds it act as the app that
# made it. Without FLAG_IMMUTABLE the holder may fill in whatever the wrapped
# Intent left blank - component, action, data, extras - and then have this app
# send it, so a notification listener or a widget host reaches a private
# activity or a content provider it could not otherwise touch. The permission
# check that would have stopped it sees this app, not the caller.
#
# The rule is the absence of the flag, which is the same question Android's own
# lint asks and the same one the platform started enforcing in API 31. It is
# asked of the flags argument as text, so `FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT or
# FLAG_IMMUTABLE` is quiet and a bare `0` is not.
#
# The flags have to be written out at the call. This is the narrowing that
# reading real code forced and it removed every false positive there was:
# LeakCanary writes `val flags = FLAG_UPDATE_CURRENT or FLAG_IMMUTABLE` a line
# above the call and Tivi writes `private const val PENDING_INTENT_FLAGS =
# FLAG_IMMUTABLE or ...` at the top of the file, so the argument this rule
# reads is a name and the decision is somewhere else. Four findings across two
# applications, four of them wrong, and all four were this. A capture that is
# a bare name says nothing about the flags, so the rule stops asking.
#
# FLAG_MUTABLE is reported even though it is deliberate. There are real uses
# for it - a direct-reply action needs the system to fill in the text - and
# there is nothing in the syntax that says which this is, so the reader decides.
# The direction that costs a false positive is better than the one that costs a
# token somebody else can aim.

["PendingIntent.$M($C, $R, $I, $F)"] as $tokens
| scan_ast("*.kt"; $tokens) as $all
| ( $all | of($tokens)
    | where_capture("M"; "^get(?:Activity|Activities|Broadcast|Service|ForegroundService)$")
    | where_capture_not("F"; "FLAG_IMMUTABLE")
    | where_capture("F"; "FLAG_[A-Z]|^[0-9]+$")
    | focus("F") )
| finding("kotlin-mutable-pending-intent";
    "these flags do not say FLAG_IMMUTABLE, so whoever is given this token can "
    + "fill in the intent and have this app send it")
| report
